---
source: src/kit.rs
expression: "info(&profiles, &made)"
---
Emergency kit of laptop, made on 2026-10-30 12:00 by me

The .toml files next to this one are the rustic profiles and passwords that open your backups: without them, the backups cannot be read. Keep this zip away from this computer, for example in a password manager or a cloud drive. Anyone with it can access your backup files.

To restore on a new computer:
1. Install rusticlone: https://github.com/AlphaJack/rusticlone#restore
2. Run: rusticlone restore --all --kit restore-kit.zip
3. Once restored, run rusticlone install --auto-update to resume your backups on this computer

Collections that this kit can restore:

Docs:
Files will be copied from /mnt/usb/Docs to /home/me/Documents.

Pictures:
Files will be copied from /mnt/usb/Pictures to /home/me/Pictures, /home/me/Videos and /home/me/Music.
If /mnt/usb/Pictures is missing, files will be copied from /Volumes/nas/Pictures instead.
If /Volumes/nas/Pictures is missing too, files will be copied from rclone:gd:Pictures instead.
